---
import { aiExample, aiSteps } from '../data/ai';
---

<section id="ai" class="relative z-10 bg-ink py-24 text-paper md:py-32">
  <div class="wrap grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] lg:gap-20">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <h2 class="display text-[clamp(2rem,4.2vw,3.6rem)] [--wdth:112] [--wght:800]">How I build with AI</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[42ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/85">
        I use Claude Code as a coding partner every day. It takes the slow parts off my hands, and I stay responsible
        for every decision and every line that ships.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-8 flex gap-6 text-sm text-steel-light" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-red"></span>Me</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue"></span>Claude</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class="text-sm text-steel-light">Example task</p>
      <p class="display mt-1 text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.4vw,2rem)] [--wdth:95] [--wght:700]">“{aiExample}”</p>

      <ol id="ai-steps" class="relative mt-10">
        <span class="absolute top-2 bottom-2 left-[5px] w-[2px] bg-paper/15" aria-hidden="true">
          <span id="ai-line" class="absolute inset-0 origin-top bg-paper/70"></span>
        </span>
        {
          aiSteps.map((s) => (
            <li class="ai-step relative pb-8 pl-10 last:pb-0">
              <span class:list={['absolute top-[0.55em] left-0 h-3 w-3 rounded-full', s.who === 'me' ? 'bg-red' : 'bg-blue']} aria-hidden="true" />
              <p class="sr-only">{s.who === 'me' ? 'Me:' : 'Claude:'}</p>
              <p class="max-w-[44ch] text-lg leading-relaxed">{s.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-12 max-w-[46ch] text-steel-light">
        The busywork goes faster, so more of my time goes into what matters: the architecture, the UX and the details.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
